          <name>fixup_13_pcrel</name>
          <briefdescription>
<para>A 12-bit PC-relative fixup for the family of branches which take 12-bit targets (RJMP,RCALL,etc). </para>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Although the fixup is labelled as 13 bits, it is actually only encoded in 12. The reason for The nonmenclature is that <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_a_v_r" kindref="compound">AVR</ref> branch targets are rightshifted by 1, because instructions are always aligned to 2 bytes, so the 0&apos;th bit is always 0. This way there is 13-bits of precision. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
